---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  name: 'Rahim Iqbal — Kerr Problems contribution record',
  url: 'https://kerrproblems.com/contributors/rahim-iqbal',
  dateModified: '2026-07-18',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    '@id': 'https://rahimiqbal.com/#person',
    name: 'Rahim Iqbal',
    url: 'https://rahimiqbal.com/',
    sameAs: [
      'https://github.com/abdulrahimiqbal',
      'https://rahimiqbal.com/projects/kerr-formalization',
    ],
  },
};
---
<Base
  title="Rahim Iqbal — Contributor"
  description="Auditable Kerr Problems contributions by Rahim Iqbal: the K-505 literature map, K-608 literature closure, and machine-checked Kerr formalization work."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData)} />

  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/about">About</a> → Contributors → Rahim Iqbal</div>
  <article class="contributor-record">
    <p class="page-meta">Contributor record</p>
    <h1>Rahim Iqbal</h1>
    <p class="contributor-deck">
      Primary-literature review, problem-status repair, and formal verification work around Kerr geometry.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>K-608 — literature closure</h2>
      <p>
        Rahim submitted the audit that closed K-608 as solved in the literature for the slowly rotating
        Kerr-de Sitter regime. The underlying nonlinear-stability theorem belongs to Hintz and Vasy, with a
        later proof by Fang; the contribution here was identifying the exact match, tightening the scope,
        recording the primary references, and separating still-open descendants.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/problems/K-608">Inspect K-608 and its references →</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="https://github.com/kerrproblems/Kerrproblems/commit/8870c15" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Audit commit ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>K-505 — documented partial advance</h2>
      <p>
        An attempted solution of the separated Teukolsky threshold-classification problem produced a
        defensible literature map rather than a false completion claim. The contribution moved K-505 from
        open to partial, documented the established nonzero-frequency and algebraically special results,
        and made the remaining zero-frequency catalog explicit.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/problems/K-505">Inspect K-505 and the remaining gap →</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="https://github.com/kerrproblems/Kerrproblems/commit/83640d2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Research-map commit ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Machine-checked Kerr work</h2>
      <p>
        In a separate Lean 4 repository, Rahim built a checked coordinate-data core for Schwarzschild and
        Kerr geometry. One narrow, directly inspectable theorem proves that the outer Kerr horizon radius is
        a root of the Kerr Delta function when the discriminant is nonnegative. The repository publishes the
        proof boundary and does not present unfinished Ricci, vacuum, or hidden-symmetry scaffolds as complete.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/abdulrahimiqbal/KerrFormalization" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Inspect the Lean repository ↗
        </a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="https://rahimiqbal.com/projects/kerr-formalization">
          Project overview ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="contributor-links">
      <a href="https://rahimiqbal.com/">Rahim Iqbal — selected work ↗</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/abdulrahimiqbal">GitHub ↗</a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>
